<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR market closed for the holidays.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR market closed for the holidays.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The market for Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) is closed on Thursday and Friday. Trading will resume on Monday.</p>
<p>PHIBOR rates were mostly higher on Wednesday following the 0.25 percentage-point increase in the U.S. interest rate.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents rates at which banks would be willing to swap their pesos for dollars.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
